  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Comparing the given equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;with a standard equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. We have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Since time period is&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mi>&#969;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>, it is a second&#39;s&nbsp;pendulum.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>99</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p>"
  }
